lucid-dock (0.1.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Icons resolve through the whole theme inheritance chain before the
    generic application icon is considered. Passing a fallback list to
    gtk_icon_theme_lookup_icon() does not mean "try these if the name is
    not found": GTK tries every name in one theme before any name in the
    theme it inherits from, so application-x-executable in Lucid beat
    google-chrome in Lucid-Everything. Nine of twelve pinned icons drew
    the generic icon; none do now.
  * The Debian package is built on the shipping target as well as on the
    development host, so ${shlibs:Depends} records the gtk4-layer-shell
    dependency. Packages built before this installed cleanly and then
    failed to start.

 -- Javid Medina <javidamedina@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 22:40:00 -0400

lucid-dock (0.1.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release.
  * Magnification driven by a single 0..1 envelope rather than per-icon
    springs, so a fast sweep magnifies exactly as much as a slow one.
  * Running applications detected through ext-foreign-toplevel-list-v1 or
    zwlr-foreign-toplevel-management-v1, falling back to /proc only where
    neither exists.
  * Geometry, motion and stylesheet values read from lucid-tokens, with
    per-key provenance, live reload and per-key reset.
  * Icons normalised to a common ink ratio, so an application shipping its
    own icon under hicolor no longer stands taller than the rest.

 -- Javid Medina <javidamedina@gmail.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0000
